The point-to-point moves on the xyzacb nutating-head sim of twp-native,
whose INI and HAL files and helpers (twp-native/native.py) it shares.

G53.4 G0 to a program point, G53.5 and G53.7 G0 to a slide position with
the head tilted, G28.5 and G30.5 to a slide position stored on the identity
kinematics, through a slide waypoint when given one, G53.4 G1 taking the
time the straight move would in G94 and in G93, and what they refuse.  The
config sets MACHINE_MOVES_IN_MACHINE_FRAME, so under TCP G53, G28 and G30 land
where G53.5, G28.5 and G30.5 do, G28.1 and G30.1 storing the slides, and on
the identity kinematics they are the world's.

The path of a move is read from a sampler on the servo thread, every cycle
of the joint commands and the world position, logged by halsampler to
samples.log while the test runs: a status snapshot per task cycle misses the
turn of a move that stops and comes back.  The log is left behind when a
check fails.
